docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2284:## §7.10 Invariant compliance
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2288:| No hidden global state | Every dependency is declared in `:yin.k/requires` — *as computed by the declared fixed point, with its completeness stated* (`:yin.k/discovery`); the store travels as an explicit slice restored into an isolated store; fresh-name state and parked records travel explicitly; custody is facts on a named, possessed medium. |
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2292:| No layer collapsing | Canonicalize, encode, discover, arbitrate, load, restore, execute are separate functions with data between them. The engine's hot loop is untouched: lifting is a pure function over the blocked machine's value, and the exporting state is that value with an emptied wait-set and a retained record — driver discipline, not engine machinery. |
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2304:## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2320:  windows of §7.7.5.
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2321:- **Pending-state completeness.** Every pending variant of §7.4.3 must
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2324:  through the aliasing scenarios of `check-wait-set`. This depends on
docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2340:  (§7.3.3): the tuple grammar — mnemonic set, per-mnemonic arity and operand
